WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.631
Week 16: Weather, Nature, and Plans. understand a forecast describe terrain change plans because of conditions

2
00:00:07.631 --> 00:00:20.193
Form and meaning. Applying the form. Combine si + present tense with another present or near-future clause to describe a likely condition and its result: si llueve, cambiamos el plan.

3
00:00:20.193 --> 00:00:45.299
Model set. Hace sol hoy, pero va a llover mañana. Si llueve, cambiamos el plan. Está nublado en la montaña. Hace mucho frío en la costa. Si hace calor, vamos a la playa. It's sunny today, but it's going to rain tomorrow. If it rains, we change the plan. It's cloudy in the mountains. It's very cold on the coast. If it's hot, we go to the beach.

4
00:00:45.299 --> 00:00:55.515
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:00:55.515 --> 00:01:08.269
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: understand a forecast; describe terrain; change plans because of conditions. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:08.269 --> 00:01:34.249
Model language. Hace sol hoy, pero va a llover mañana. — It's sunny today, but it's going to rain tomorrow. Si llueve, cambiamos el plan. — If it rains, we change the plan. Está nublado en la montaña. — It's cloudy in the mountains. Hace mucho frío en la costa. — It's very cold on the coast. Si hace calor, vamos a la playa. — If it's hot, we go to the beach.

7
00:01:34.249 --> 00:01:44.169
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
